WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 11.15 · Fundraising, Revenue & Sustainable Business Models
Funder and customer mapping and prospect research

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Research fit and evidence first; prioritise a few prospects and rule out poor fits.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Check priorities, eligibility, size and timing at the source.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Record where and when you found each fact.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Score, shortlist, and decide not to approach when fit is weak.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Tide Line Youth Collective (Community group · idea stage, Indonesia)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Tide Line: high priority for dive operator A and the village funds; do not approach the resort that cleared mangroves.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You build a short, evidence-based prospect list.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
